"Not every old pigment is safe. Lead white contains lead. Vermilion is made from cinnabar, which contains mercury. Gamboge, a yellow tree resin used in Chinese painting, is also poisonous. Over time, safer pigments such as titanium white took the place of some of these. Today the paints made for schools are chosen with safety in mind, but you should still wash your hands and never eat or drink while you paint.": "bb0ae5866cb9",
